3. Implement a basic infection routine that copies the virus into the MBR, MBR, or partition table of any connected storage devices.

4. Add a self-replication mechanism, so that when the infected computer boots up, the virus code executes and spreads to other partitions or storage devices.

5. Test the virus by booting from an infected storage device and observing if it successfully infects the MBR and spreads.


